These assert statements will check the conditions defined in the comments. If the conditions are not met, the program will fail and possibly throw an exception. This feature is often used for debugging, as it allows programmers to specify that certain conditions should always be true, helping them to catch and fix bugs early in their development process.--------------------
Debug.Assert(templatesFileExist);
</code>

Explanation: 
The comment "@@@ the template file exists" became the assert condition "templatesFileExist == true" because the existence check is already a boolean condition. The condition checks whether the file exists and if it exists Debug.Assert will pass, otherwise it will fail indicating a problem with the templates file existence check.--------------------
